Now when we delete we simply need to change the index of the thing we're swapping in; it's ID doesn't change.Â 

The last thing we need to address for stability is the generation. So we have our swapped entity and our reference is still stable, but what about our old reference to the thing we deleted? We want to know that that isn't valid anymore. We use the generation for this. Think of it like "how many times have I used this information". When you delete something we increment the generation for that info, so now when we look up an entity handle we want to make sure the handle's generation matches the info's.Â 

When we delete an entity now we want to increase the generation so we invalidate all handles to it, and we want to add the id to the freelist so we can keep track of which entities to use.

